      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $‖u‖=7$ and $u\\cdot v=21$, find the smallest possible value of $‖2v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |21| & \\le 7\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 3 & \\le 2\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 6 & \\le ‖2v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖2v‖$ is $6.$",
